{
  "_comment": "A plaza fountain, after the one in Viterbo's Piazza San Pellegrino: two round steps, a waisted drum (a hyperboloid) with an overhanging rim, holding water; a cluster of columns standing in it carrying a tazza (a paraboloid shell) of water, a waisted neck (a hyperboloid again), a small cup of water and a finial (a spheroid). Each body of water is a plane carrying the water inside a shape that only divides, set a hair inside the marble round it, so no ray meets that shape and the water's env is the water alone. The waters come last in the group, so they fill round what stands in them.",
